  "scope": "Paper30 Section02 only: three coupled formula/argument readings and the synchronized local producer projection.",
  "summary": "Restore the distinction between the ordinary coefficient b_l and Fraktur ideals in the minimal-length argument, and restore the source-order alpha expansion. The earlier legitimate Fraktur ideal congruence remains unchanged.",
  "human_auditable_considerations": {
    "question": "Whether the three inherited Russian Paper30 readings preserve the source's distinction between a coefficient and its associated ideals.",
    "evidence_weighed": [
      "ED0014 lines 14797 and 14802 distinguish ordinary b_l from Fraktur ideals and give alpha=a_1 xi_1+...+b_l xi_l.",
      "The accepted P30b adjudication, checker, and primary-print receipt independently bind the same readings.",
      "The earlier sentence's Fraktur b_i congruent 0 modulo Fraktur a_i is a legitimate ideal-to-ideal relation and serves as a negative control."
    ],
    "alternatives_rejected": [
      "Globally replace Fraktur b in the paragraph: most occurrences name ideals and must remain Fraktur.",
      "Repair only the expansion or only one congruence: the three loci form one coupled contradiction argument and partial repair leaves it incoherent.",
      "Retranslate surrounding Russian prose or infer native-language certification from generated corpus witnesses."
    ],
    "uncertainty": "The mathematical/source distinction is directly controlled. The bounded Russian wording is retained from the edition; no native/community review or critical-edition certification is claimed."
  },
